portable-pi
===========

This project is a rewrite for pi (pi-coding-agent) of the ideas and the
USB-drive layout pioneered by:

    portable-agent-usb
    https://github.com/bnovik0v/portable-agent-usb
    MIT License, Copyright (c) 2026

Upstream ships Claude Code and OpenAI Codex on a USB stick. It is not a git fork:
portable-pi shares no commits with it and no source file is copied verbatim.
What was reused:

  * the overall idea and directory layout (bin/<platform>, tools/<platform>,
    config/, temp/ plus a per-OS launcher);
  * the "no traces on the host" approach: redirect the agent config directory,
    the temp directory and the package caches onto the drive;
  * the launcher convention of detecting the drive root from the script path;
  * the exFAT choice and its documented consequences;
  * the autorun.inf pattern (volume label only: modern Windows ignores AutoRun
    programs on removable media).

Everything else is new work for a different agent: manifest-driven builds,
Node.js 24 LTS payload, MinGit instead of PortableGit (94 MB / 376 files instead
of 392 MB / 9,622), an agent-dir override for pi, explicit skill mounting through
`-ns --skill`, the isolation verifier, the self-contained updater, the
cross-platform (Windows + Linux) payload, and the bundled agent instructions.

The MIT license of the upstream project is reproduced below to keep the
attribution intact.

